r-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289812}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b2050e06-0476-56c1-a7a1-1d0ef234a4b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-24642" :question/problem "$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can simplify the given expression by rewriting the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ in the denominator, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}}{2\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060243 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93710ca5-6027-591d-969f-097bebd99547" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\sin (\\frac{π}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058101} {:answer/id #uuid "dafb79ee-0595-52df-b01e-9c1753d35db9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\sin (\\frac{π}{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058102} {:answer/id #uuid "e1131cf8-b01f-5702-9ca2-a730156984f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\sin (\\frac{π}{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058103} {:answer/id #uuid "3af60303-8273-5e10-9f8e-89a0cc111a4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sin (\\frac{π}{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058104} {:answer/id #uuid "7b156a1e-b747-5820-8472-2b68ebe1b1db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin (\\frac{π}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058105}] :answer-field/id #uuid "df1354db-d1d7-54db-baba-68ca0802536b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058100}] :question/id #uuid "0ab58d1b-4097-516b-91bf-48c130e66ed2" :question/math-academy-id "q-24648" :question/problem "What is $6\\sin (\\frac{π}{12})\\cos (\\frac{π}{12})\\cos (\\frac{π}{6})$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060246 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "362fffeb-2576-5d58-b4ac-2e8e14f21e76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427521} {:answer/id #uuid "722eb547-e288-5ad4-ab49-790d9559959d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427523} {:answer/id #uuid "e642531e-a868-556f-a278-25243d434fda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427528} {:answer/id #uuid "ecae479f-b48b-5f1e-97cb-6dff17dcea7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427529} {:answer/id #uuid "f499bdbb-1a30-5059-8d7c-e95901e28a16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427530}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e642531e-a868-556f-a278-25243d434fda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427528} :answer-field/id #uuid "0114138c-2ef8-582d-af73-d2fbea6e795c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058113}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a899c299-0869-5669-9b1c-ab47bfeb6793" :question/math-academy-id "q-24760" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-1)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\n-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's take a look at the unit circle.\n\n![](images/db/dbf36192ac332dc49ed75278838e989a37ac7d888311be1b8b059a7b59667aa6.png)\n\nFrom the values on the unit circle, we see that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})=-1.\n$$\n\nHowever, $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ does not lie within the range of $\\theta .$ To get an angle that's coterminal with $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ that lies within the range of $\\theta ,$ we subtract $2\\pi .$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\pi }{2}-2\\pi =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-1)=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060247 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "026c76c0-a12a-530d-8ce5-beb75dbbf1fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288048} {:answer/id #uuid "4611eebe-f433-56f5-a87d-1387b39dc76d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288510} {:answer/id #uuid "c2e7c13d-0b7e-5e9a-b6f7-91a103d2b81e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289320} {:answer/id #uuid "ccd20ff6-854f-5350-875d-857afc14bca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289394} {:answer/id #uuid "d0d88f34-c80b-54d2-882a-2d5c52516bc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289421}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0d88f34-c80b-54d2-882a-2d5c52516bc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289421} :answer-field/id #uuid "05376533-2b05-5f6d-a2b1-6461515cb1ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289738}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2cbce6d6-52b3-5bc8-a814-978defb5db2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-24770" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\n-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's take a look at the unit circle.\n\n![](images/db/dbf36192ac332dc49ed75278838e989a37ac7d888311be1b8b059a7b59667aa6.png)\n\nFrom the values in the unit circle, we see that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{11\\pi }{6})=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nHowever, $\\frac{11\\pi }{6}$ does not lie within the range of $\\theta .$ To get an angle that's coterminal with $\\frac{11\\pi }{6}$ that lies within the range of $\\theta ,$ we subtract $2\\pi .$\n\n$$\n\\frac{11\\pi }{6}-2\\pi =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060249 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33f0f137-c430-5061-9aba-b7129465682e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288376} {:answer/id #uuid "35864b6e-3160-54c7-bb0e-bbc1a3db4cf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288392} {:answer/id #uuid "4b2e4678-898e-5968-8e8e-f42eee7f8c22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288553} {:answer/id #uuid "9b91da1b-cbc8-5cbe-9932-fdd206c48a34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289077} {:answer/id #uuid "dc2818c1-253d-5758-83e4-f0b3910f6f07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35864b6e-3160-54c7-bb0e-bbc1a3db4cf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288392} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b668a88-94da-5c15-92cb-0b1782d6eb86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290033}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9f5ad5b9-cf75-5c20-a9c5-6e5d15578fe2" :question/math-academy-id "q-24788" :question/problem "Find the exact value of ${(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}))}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parenthesis and use the Pythagorean identity.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}))}^{2} & ={sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =[{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})]-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =1-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) & =1-(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}))}^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060250 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02f71a90-9f0c-57a8-8d03-9d9eeaccc52b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288051} {:answer/id #uuid "443aa495-57ed-5721-9745-6ff07a7e846d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288496} {:answer/id #uuid "81913624-dd8d-5e6e-a115-a31409962017" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288905} {:answer/id #uuid "8bd93056-9bf4-54d1-81ae-7be48a7ed21a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288965} {:answer/id #uuid "df916113-228a-55af-a94b-2a8acc6b6b99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289523}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8bd93056-9bf4-54d1-81ae-7be48a7ed21a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288965} :answer-field/id #uuid "574749d6-30f1-54d9-a75b-edfe46306402" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289913}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d044bebd-f049-585d-81d1-00fe08c3d294" :question/math-academy-id "q-24911" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=$" :question/worked-solution "The range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\n0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi .\n$$\n\nNote that the angle $\\theta $ spans the first and second quadrants.\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ is negative, our answer is an angle that lies in the second quadrant, where cosine is negative.\n\n![](images/db/dbf36192ac332dc49ed75278838e989a37ac7d888311be1b8b059a7b59667aa6.png)\n\nFrom the values in the second quadrant, we see that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060281 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25359b67-eaea-5841-87ea-41c51d80e042" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327256} {:answer/id #uuid "472a4c79-8034-5837-9d05-873c816b4e72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327554} {:answer/id #uuid "96b357da-cd50-58ad-91cb-c377a5bc9072" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328241} {:answer/id #uuid "c0765f72-cfed-50b4-a56b-2a85321c3992" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328615} {:answer/id #uuid "d29bac5b-368f-5a8e-9513-132bb1b8af10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25359b67-eaea-5841-87ea-41c51d80e042" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327256} :answer-field/id #uuid "00e02698-834f-5f8e-bbf7-5a260377acd9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329185}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f043b7ca-be08-556b-94ec-1d757642bb0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-43383" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060313 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "978e39c1-7224-55ec-97ef-131b7529f199" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21000 \\cdot (\\frac{5}{6})^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058501} {:answer/id #uuid "e4364e89-dc6a-5e17-a089-46dbf11d7eb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21000^{4} \\cdot (\\frac{5}{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058502} {:answer/id #uuid "f98649bc-67d1-526a-a56a-0d7455c89ec5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21000^{4} \\cdot (\\frac{1}{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058503} {:answer/id #uuid "3076692b-6855-55c0-be76-19e0537c5ab3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21000 \\cdot (\\frac{7}{6})^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058504} {:answer/id #uuid "65b5ae26-ea6b-5996-90d9-b36a2a0b6c1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21000 \\cdot (\\frac{1}{6})^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058505}] :answer-field/id #uuid "d479c863-639d-56a4-9071-5f0cff471293" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058500}] :question/id #uuid "2bee8798-e2b3-5c90-8671-0f08970da973" :question/math-academy-id "q-61853" :question/problem "There are $21000$ rhinos left in the wild. If the population of rhinos decreases by $\\frac{1}{6}$ every year, which 